Receipts builds on published research by Meta and others; the "Prior work and what is new here" section of README.md lists each source. Falden, Inc. is not affiliated with Meta, and Meta has not endorsed Receipts.

The differential attacker's prompt, in src/receipts/attack/differential.py, quotes Testora's five questions verbatim (Pradel, ICSE 2026, arXiv:2503.18597v3, https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.18597v3).

Third-party material

The files below contain material from other sources. Falden, Inc.'s license above does not cover it; it stays under its sources' own terms.

- demo/pandas-64677/patch.diff, fix.diff and target.template.json, and the run and fix records under demo/pandas-64677/evidence/: code and pull-request text from pandas (https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas), which is licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License. pandas' license text is in demo/pandas-64677/LICENSE.pandas.
- eval/pilot-run.jsonl, eval/pilot.json, eval/sample.json, eval/sample-provisional.json, eval/manifest.json, eval/test-specs.json, eval/pools/ and tests/attack/fixtures/: issue texts and agent patches from SWE-bench Verified and the SWE-bench experiments repository, which state no license; code from the upstream projects those patches change, under each project's own license (see "Upstream project code" below); and labels and the pool of 251 instances, both derived from SWE-ABS (arXiv:2603.00520v1), whose repository is under the MIT License and whose dataset is under the Apache License 2.0.
- The final's target summaries in eval/final/targets/: issue texts from SWE-bench Verified, which states no license; each target's template claim that its issue is fixed quotes the issue in full.
- src/receipts/eval/labelrun.py: apply_files and remove_conflicting_chunks adapt SWE-ABS's get_apply_files and remove_conflicting_chunks (swe-bench/swebench/harness/utils.py in https://github.com/OpenAgentEval/SWE-ABS at revision 26b4c736), under the MIT License (notice below).
- eval/test-specs.json, and the NON_TEST_EXTS and LOG_PARSERS constants in src/receipts/eval/specs.py: install and test commands for each repository version, and those two constants, from the SWE-bench harness, swebench 4.1.0 (https://github.com/SWE-bench/SWE-bench), under the MIT License (notice below). The harness's logic is also adapted, with credit in comments, in harness_test_files in src/receipts/eval/specs.py, harness_label in src/receipts/attack/runners.py (get_test_directives), answers in src/receipts/contracts.py (the log parsers' id renames), PATCH_CHAIN in src/receipts/eval/runsc_check.py and HARNESS_CHAIN in src/receipts/attack/sandbox.py (GIT_APPLY_CMDS).

